{"step_index":241,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-06T13:30:35Z","thinking":"**Adding User Role Banner**\n\nThe plan is to insert a User Role and Permission Status Banner into `dashboard.html`. This banner will sit above the existing tabs. It uses HTML for structure and inline CSS for basic styling, including a flexbox layout, a contrasting left border, and some padding and margin to give it visual separation from surrounding elements.\n\n\n**Implementing User Role-Based UI**\n\nThe application logic now requires conditional UI element display based on user roles. Specifically, the \"Verifier\" role hides several tabs and buttons, displaying a specific role banner, while the \"Institution\" role shows the qualifications registry and issuance buttons, hiding the telemetry tab. The role-specific UI configuration is implemented in Javascript. The UI also needs to adjust table row button visibility.\n\n\n**Deducing User Role-Based Privileges**\n\nExamining role-based conditional logic reveals that a \"Registrar Officer\" role restricts credential revocation, hides the telemetry tab, and adjusts the banner displayed. The \"Admin\" role grants full access, including revocation authority, visible telemetry tab, and a different banner presentation. The UI's behavior is explicitly controlled via Javascript, based on `user.role` from local storage.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Madziva\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\qualification-verification-system\\\\src\\\\main\\\\java\\\\com\\\\devops\\\\qvs\\\\service\\\\AiFraudDetectionService.java\"","EndLine":"227","StartLine":"150","toolAction":"\"Viewing AiFraudDetectionService chat\"","toolSummary":"\"Check processUserQuery in AiFraudDetectionService\""}}]}
